{"id": "section-body-27580", "title": "Wernicke’s Encephalopathy", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-three", "blocks": [{"id": "body-27580", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Wernicke’s Encephalopathy", "runs": [{"text": "Wernicke’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Encephalopathy"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "359"}}, {"id": "body-27581", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Wernicke’s Encephalopathy (WE) is an acute neuropsychiatric syndrome that results from thiamine deficiency. It is linked to significant morbidity and mortality. If untreated, it can progress to Korsakoff Syndrome, which is characterized by a disproportionate impairment in memory compared to other cognitive functions. Common causes include a staple diet of unpolished rice, chronic alcohol abuse, malnutrition, recurrent vomiting and diarrhoea, gastrointestinal surgery, magnesium deficiency, unbalanced nutrition, cancer, and chemotherapeutic treatments.", "runs": [{"text": "Wernicke’s Encephalopathy (WE) is an acute neuropsychiatric syndrome that results from thiamine deficiency. It is linked to significant morbidity and mortality. If untreated, it can progress to Korsakoff Syndrome, which is characterized by a disproportionate impairment in memory compared to other cognitive functions. Common causes include a staple diet of unpolished rice, chronic alcohol abuse, malnutrition, recurrent vomiting and diarrhoea, gastrointestinal surgery, magnesium deficiency, unbalanced nutrition, cancer, and chemotherapeutic treatments."}]}, {"id": "body-27583", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27584", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "May present with relatively non-specific Common symptoms or signs include:", "runs": [{"text": "May"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "present"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relatively"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non-specific"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Common"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include:"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27585", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Ocular abnormalities", "runs": [{"text": "Ocular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abnormalities"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27586", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Mental status changes (Delirium)", "runs": [{"text": "Mental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "status"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "changes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Delirium)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27587", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Incoordination and gait ataxia", "runs": [{"text": "Incoordination"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gait"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ataxia"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27588", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Other symptoms include", "runs": [{"text": "Other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27589", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Hypotension and tachycardia", "runs": [{"text": "Hypotension"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tachycardia"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27590", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Seizures", "runs": [{"text": "Seizures"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27591", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Hearing loss", "runs": [{"text": "Hearing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loss"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27592", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Hypothermia", "runs": [{"text": "Hypothermia"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27593", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Late-stage symptoms include Hyperthermia, Increased muscle tone, spastic paresis, Choreic dyskinesia, Coma", "runs": [{"text": "Late-stage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hyperthermia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Increased"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "muscle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tone,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spastic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "paresis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Choreic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dyskinesia,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Coma"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "319"}}, {"id": "body-27595", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Management", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27596", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: thiamine hydrochloride 500mg dissolved in 100ml of NS given by infusion over 30 minutes, 8 hourly for 3 days. If an effective response is observed,", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "thiamine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hydrochloride"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dissolved"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "100ml"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "NS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "given"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infusion"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "over"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "minutes,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "3"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days. If an effective response is observed,"}]}, {"id": "body-27597", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading3", "text": "THEN", "runs": [{"text": "THEN"}], "level": 3}, {"id": "body-27598", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: thiamine 250mg IV/IM daily for 5 days,", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "thiamine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "250mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "IV/IM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days,"}]}, {"id": "body-27600", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Prophylactic treatment in people with alcohol intoxication, severe alcohol withdrawal and people with poor diet and signs of malnutrition:", "runs": [{"text": "Prophylactic treatment in people with alcohol intoxication, severe alcohol withdrawal and people with poor diet and signs of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malnutrition:"}]}, {"id": "body-27601", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: thiamine 250mg IM once daily for 3-5 consecutive days.", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "thiamine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "250mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "IM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "once"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "3-5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "consecutive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days."}]}, {"id": "body-27602", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading3", "text": "THEN", "runs": [{"text": "THEN"}], "level": 3}, {"id": "body-27603", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: thiamine 100mg (PO)daily for at least 3 months.", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "thiamine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "100mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "least"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "3"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "months."}]}, {"id": "body-27604", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Give Thiamine before or concomitantly with intravenous administration of glucose if WE is suspected, as glucose alone can precipitate the disorder in thiamine-deficient individuals.", "runs": [{"text": "Give Thiamine before or concomitantly with intravenous administration of glucose if WE is suspected, as glucose alone can precipitate the disorder in thiamine-deficient individuals."}]}, {"id": "body-27606", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Management of vitamin b12 deficiency with neuropsychiatric symptoms", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vitamin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "b12"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deficiency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neuropsychiatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}]}, {"id": "body-27607", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: hydroxocobalamin (IM) 1mg 24hourly for 1 week, then weekly for 4 weeks, then monthly thereafter until maximum improvement has occurred.", "runs": [{"text": "S: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "hydroxocobalamin (IM) 1mg 24hourly for 1 week, then weekly for 4 weeks, then monthly thereafter until maximum improvement has occurred."}]}, {"id": "body-27608", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-27609", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: methyl cobalamin 500µgm (PO) 8hrly until maximum improvement has been observed. Stop if the underlying cause is corrected.", "runs": [{"text": "S: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "methyl cobalamin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500µgm (PO) 8hrly until maximum improvement has been observed."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Stop if the underlying cause is "}, {"text": "corrected."}]}, {"id": "body-27610", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "AND", "runs": [{"text": "AND"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-27611", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: folic acid (PO) 2mg once two weeks after starting treatment.", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "folic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "once"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "two"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "starting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment."}]}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Mental health conditions", "start": "body-27580", "end": "body-27611"}}